C2","gene_id":"ENSG00000064270","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.724514,"donor_log2fc":-0.247686,"donor_lfcse":0.14967,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.0054612,"degas_log2fc":null,"degas_padj":null},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_symbol":"ATP2C2","gene_symbol_current":"ATP2C2","gene_id":"ENSG00000064270","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"unclear","nucleus_padj":0.913981,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.0310155,"nucleus_score":0.175684,"pct_ad":0.349687,"pct_control":0.34276,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999342,"donor_log2fc":-0.175449,"donor_lfcse":0.240436,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-4.86446e-05,"degas_log2fc":-0.559748,"degas_padj":2.903e-32},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"ATP2C2","gene_symbol_current":"ATP2C2","gene_id":"ENSG00000064270","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.883982,"donor_log2fc":-0.143347,"donor_lfcse":0.170783,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.00538982,"degas_log2fc":null,"degas_padj":null}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ex","gene_id":"ENSG00000064270","module":"greenyellow","kme":0.727601,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.398964,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_id":"ENSG00000064270","module":"yellow","kme":0.189606,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.663532,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000064270","entrez_id":["9914"],"uniprot":["O75185"],"ncbi_summary":"Enables P-type calcium transporter activity and P-type manganese transporter activity. Predicted to be involved in calcium ion transmembrane transport; cellular calcium ion homeostasis; and manganese ion transport. Predicted to act upstream of or within mammary gland epithelium development; positive regulation of calcium ion import; and protein localization to plasma membrane. Predicted to be located in trans-Golgi network membrane. Predicted to be active in Golgi membrane; endoplasmic reticulum; and plasma membrane. Predicted to be integral component of membrane. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"O75185","text":"ATP-driven pump that supplies the Golgi apparatus with Ca(2+) and Mn(2+) ions, both essential cofactors for processing and trafficking of newly synthesized proteins in the secretory pathway (PubMed:15677451, PubMed:15831496, PubMed:16332677, PubMed:30923126). Within a catalytic cycle, acquires Ca(2+) or Mn(2+) ions on the cytoplasmic side of the membrane and delivers them to the lumenal side. The transfer of ions across the membrane is coupled to ATP hydrolysis and is associated with a transient phosphorylation that shifts the pump conformation from inward-facing to outward-facing state (PubMed:15831496, PubMed:16332677). Induces Ca(2+) influx independently of its ATP-driven pump function. At the basolateral membrane of mammary epithelial cells, interacts with Ca(2+) channel ORAI1 and mediates Ca(2+) entry independently of the Ca(2+) content of endoplasmic reticulum or Golgi stores. May facilitate transepithelial transport of large quantities of Ca(2+) for milk secretion via activation of Ca(2+) influx channels at the plasma membrane and active Ca(2+) transport at the Golgi apparatus (PubMed:20887894, PubMed:23840669)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}